# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Lead table (website enquiries) lives in Prisma Postgres, which exposes the
# same database under two connection strings. BOTH variables below are required
# — the schema references each one, and a missing DIRECT_DATABASE_URL fails the
# build. Get them from https://console.prisma.io → your database → Connect.
# The credential is inside each URL, so treat the whole string as a secret.

# Runtime queries. Use the Accelerate URL in any serverless deployment.
# Serverless instances freeze between requests, which silently kills a raw TCP
# connection pool; the next query then waits out the pool timeout and fails with
# "Timed out fetching a new connection from the connection pool". Accelerate is
# HTTP, so it has no pool to go stale. src/lib/db.ts already applies
# withAccelerate(), which is a no-op against a plain postgres:// URL.
DATABASE_URL="prisma+postgres://accelerate.prisma-data.net/?api_key=REPLACE_ME"

# Migrations. The migration engine speaks raw Postgres and cannot go through
# Accelerate, so `prisma migrate deploy` (which `bun run build` runs) uses this.
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgres://USER:PASSWORD@pooled.db.prisma.io:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"

# ─── Enquiry notifications (Resend) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Leads are always saved to the database. These values switch on the email
# that tells someone a new lead has arrived.
#
#   1. Sign up at https://resend.com — the free tier covers 3,000 emails/month
#   2. Add a domain under Domains and add the DNS records it gives you
#   3. Create an API key and paste it below
#
# Without RESEND_API_KEY and QUOTE_NOTIFY_FROM the site still works: enquiries
# are stored and logged with a warning, but nobody is emailed.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The sender. Must be an address on a domain verified in THIS Resend account —
# it does not have to be the company's own domain. This mail is an internal
# "you have a new lead" notice, not customer-facing, and notify.ts sets replyTo
# to the customer's address so replying reaches them rather than the sender.
QUOTE_NOTIFY_FROM="Borotho Tafoleng Website <website@your-verified-domain.co.za>"

# Where new enquiries land. Any address — no verification needed on this side.
# Defaults to COMPANY.email in src/lib/constants.ts, which is still a
# placeholder, so set this explicitly until the company mailbox exists.
QUOTE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
